fact WorkItem(id: "WI-646", description: some(value: "Simp rewriter convergence follow-up (efficiency + DRY after WI-643 united the term/occurrence carriers onto one iterative Value-carrier driver). Five items, all in rustland/anthill-core (resolve.rs + simp_rewrite.rs), no behavior change intended: (1) A CORRECT O(1) simp-firing gate as a KB-cached bit computed at load — mirror equation_is_directional_rewrite ([simp] OR [unfold]) over BOTH eq and unify functors, so apply_eq_rules can short-circuit a no-directional-rewrite KB WITHOUT the per-call rules_by_functor bucket scan (2 Vec allocs) that made WI-643's naive gate net-negative, and WITHOUT the [simp]-only/eq-only bug that silently skipped unfold-only or <=>-only KBs (WI-643 removed that gate entirely rather than ship it wrong). (2) Gather the eq+unify simp rule-id list ONCE per simp_rewrite::rewrite walk and thread it into the SimpFirer, instead of fire_simp_equation/try_fire re-gathering rules_by_functor(eq)+rules_by_functor(unify) at EVERY node (amplified by WI-641/643 per-node firing). (3) Extract the triplicated eq+unify selection (has_simp_equations + fire_simp_equation + try_fire all spell 'rids = rules_by_functor(eq); if unify != eq { extend(rules_by_functor(unify)) }') into ONE simp_equation_rids(kb) helper so the gate can never drift from the fire sites again — that drift is exactly what caused the WI-643 regression (has_simp_equations was eq-only while the fire sites scan eq+unify). (4) Give reassemble_value's Value::Term arm an unchanged-check (compare rewritten children to the originals by TermId, like the Node arm's ChildCursor.changed/Rc::ptr_eq) so it skips kb.alloc(Term::Fn) + the two SmallVec builds on an unchanged subtree — now hit on every node since WI-643 removed the fuel-as-depth cutoff. (5) Fix the pre-existing has_simp_equations eq-only + [simp]-only narrowness that leaves the typer's simp_enabled (typing.rs; simp_enabled = has_simp_equations(kb) || kb.has_dot_applies) UNDER-firing for a KB whose [simp] laws are all <=>-headed (the stdlib case: 14/14) and which has no dot-applies. REF: WI-643 (Phase 3, driver unification), WI-641 (Phase 2), WI-640 (Phase 1). Rust-only. Found by /code-review during WI-643."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-643"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "opus-wi646", at: "2026-07-05T22:19:02Z"))

